# A second wave of Go stdlib CVEs landed after the entries above were written. These hit
# every statically compiled Go binary in the image at once — gosu 1.19 (go1.24.6), yq
# v4.53.3 (go1.26.4), and gh 2.97.0 (go1.26.5). All three are the latest upstream release
# (verified via GitHub API 2026-08-16); none has been rebuilt against a patched toolchain
# yet, so there is no version to bump to. CVE-2026-46600 additionally shows up as
# golang.org/x/net v0.55.0 vendored into yq — same story, fixed by a yq rebuild we don't
# control. Re-review 2026-11-01.
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-46600
CVE-2026-56853
CVE-2026-56858
CVE-2026-56859
CVE-2026-56860
CVE-2026-56862

# npm 12.0.1's own bundled brace-expansion (5.0.7, under
# /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/) carries this CVE. `npm install -g
# npm@12.0.2` (the only newer patch available as of 2026-08-01) does not replace it —
# npm's self-upgrade leaves its own currently-running install directory untouched, a
# known npm limitation, not something this Dockerfile can force. Not our code to patch
# directly; tracked for the next Node/npm version bump. Re-review 2026-11-01.
CVE-2026-14257

# Same npm-bundled-dependency situation as above, found in the 2026-08-16 scan: a newer
# brace-expansion CVE plus one in ip-address 10.2.0, both under npm's own
# /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/. Neither is in
# npm-lockfiles/claude-code/package-lock.json, so regenerating that lockfile does not
# reach them, and node 22.23.2 is the latest 22.x (verified 2026-08-16) — there is no
# Node bump available that ships a patched npm bundle. Re-review 2026-11-01.
CVE-2026-69152
CVE-2026-69192
